WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.097 --> 00:00:01.134
- And also, you're not supposed

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:03.528
to have a girlfriend until you're 35.

00:00:03.528 --> 00:00:06.361
(energetic music)

00:00:08.085 --> 00:00:10.712
- She is loving, but very strict.

00:00:10.712 --> 00:00:12.525
- She's constantly moving,
constantly working,

00:00:12.525 --> 00:00:14.333
constantly offering you food.

00:00:14.333 --> 00:00:15.461
- I would say my mom is wild.

00:00:15.461 --> 00:00:18.461
She's very energetic and very silly.

00:00:19.444 --> 00:00:20.343
- She can yell.

00:00:20.343 --> 00:00:22.941
Like, across a football stadium.

00:00:22.941 --> 00:00:24.037
"Sissy Joanne!"

00:00:24.037 --> 00:00:25.535
- What have I done in my past life

00:00:25.535 --> 00:00:26.809
to deserve this? (chuckles)

00:00:26.809 --> 00:00:27.759
- She'd be like, "Huh?"

00:00:27.759 --> 00:00:30.168
- "Huh? What did you say?

00:00:30.168 --> 00:00:31.125
"Can you say that again?

00:00:31.125 --> 00:00:32.910
"Say that to your mother."

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:34.116
- I always just figured I would never date

00:00:34.116 --> 00:00:35.586
when I was in high school,

00:00:35.586 --> 00:00:37.159
or that if I was gonna do it, I'd have

00:00:37.159 --> 00:00:38.882
to do it in secret behind her back.

00:00:38.882 --> 00:00:40.202
- They want you to focus on schoolwork,

00:00:40.202 --> 00:00:41.720
and then by 25, they're like,

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.005
"What's wrong with you?" (chuckles)

00:00:43.005 --> 00:00:44.241
- "Kevin, if you had a girlfriend,

00:00:44.241 --> 00:00:45.624
"you would tell me, right?"

00:00:45.624 --> 00:00:47.753
I'm just like, "Yeah, sure."

00:00:47.753 --> 00:00:48.950
- "You don't need any
other man in your life

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:50.260
"besides your father."

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:51.299
- Discussions with my mom about dating

00:00:51.299 --> 00:00:54.137
were basically nonexistent.

00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:55.469
- When I go shopping
with her, she'll be like,

00:00:55.469 --> 00:00:56.737
"Nothing past $10."

00:00:56.737 --> 00:00:57.697
- My mom has basically taught me

00:00:57.697 --> 00:00:59.664
that I don't have to pay
anything at full price.

00:00:59.664 --> 00:01:01.632
- "You have a shirt just like that, Sissy.

00:01:01.632 --> 00:01:02.829
"Why would you spend any more money

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:04.632
"on another shirt like that?"

00:01:04.632 --> 00:01:06.042
- "Kevin, you need to
think about the family.

00:01:06.042 --> 00:01:07.572
"It's not just about you."

00:01:07.572 --> 00:01:09.704
- Up until college, I wore exclusively

00:01:09.704 --> 00:01:11.902
JCPenney clothes.

00:01:11.902 --> 00:01:14.650
- With career, my mom
was just always like,

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:16.244
"Are you sure you don't
want to be a nurse?"

00:01:16.244 --> 00:01:17.975
- "Well, you studied something Englishy.

00:01:17.975 --> 00:01:19.096
"You could go to law school."

00:01:19.096 --> 00:01:20.092
- When my mom met my roommate,

00:01:20.092 --> 00:01:21.556
who is a programmer, she was like,

00:01:21.556 --> 00:01:23.948
"Chris could have been a programmer too.

00:01:23.948 --> 00:01:25.292
"He majored in programming, but you know,

00:01:25.292 --> 00:01:26.477
he's not a programmer." (chuckles)

00:01:26.477 --> 00:01:28.221
- "You know, you should
get your master's degree.

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:29.597
"Oh, you know, there's still time

00:01:29.597 --> 00:01:30.866
"to be a pharmacist."

00:01:30.866 --> 00:01:32.254
- "Doctor" still gets thrown around.

00:01:32.254 --> 00:01:34.100
- "Oh, why don't you become a doctor?"

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.337
- She wanted me to grow in her footsteps

00:01:36.337 --> 00:01:38.069
and do that same career, but it never

00:01:38.069 --> 00:01:39.560
really worked out, and I think

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:41.012
she just got over it after a while.

00:01:41.012 --> 00:01:41.876
- Sometimes moms just have a hard time

00:01:41.876 --> 00:01:44.218
accepting the fact that
they can't help you

00:01:44.218 --> 00:01:45.418
with everything.

00:01:45.418 --> 00:01:47.014
I think that's also a
really good opportunity

00:01:47.014 --> 00:01:48.708
for you to bond with each other.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.078
- I'd resented it when I was younger,

00:01:50.078 --> 00:01:53.558
but I appreciate it now, and
I wouldn't change anything.

00:01:53.558 --> 00:01:54.839
- And so I don't think
I could ever thank her

00:01:54.839 --> 00:01:57.064
enough for just always looking out for me

00:01:57.064 --> 00:01:59.572
and making sure that
had my head on straight,

00:01:59.572 --> 00:02:02.031
had money in my pocket,
and my stomach was full.

00:02:02.031 --> 00:02:04.864
(energetic music)

